{"availability":"available","full":"mneuhaus/wall-e-dora","name":"wall-e-dora","description":"Dora-based control stack for a custom WALL-E robot with tracked drive, SC-series servos, camera features, diagnostics, and a mobile-first web UI.","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":12,"forks":3,"created":"2025-02-07T22:09:23Z","updated":"2026-03-15T18:21:50Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mneuhaus.github.io/wall-e-dora/","topics":["cm4","dora","embedded","github-pages","maker","opencv","raspberry-pi","robotics","servo","wall-e"],"demo":"https://mneuhaus.github.io/wall-e-dora/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:46:01.133Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:46:01.133Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:46:01.133Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:04:23.750Z","stars":12,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-17T22:39:49.059Z","stars":12,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-19T13:46:01.133Z","stars":12,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Mini demo video · Node reference · Build log photos · GitHub Discussions · Onshape CAD","WALL-E-DORA is a Dora-based robot control stack for a WALL-E-inspired build running on a Raspberry Pi CM4 with a Waveshare CM4-NANO-B carrier board plus an RP2040 motor controller. It combines a mobile-friendly web UI, audio playback, eye animations, tracked movement, servo animation, battery monitoring, camera features, and choreographed action sequences into one modular system.","This is not a polished general-purpose robotics kit. It is my firmware/software stack for my own WALL-E build. You are absolutely welcome to use it, study it, fork it, and adapt it for your own robot, but please do not expect product-level support, hand-holding, or guaranteed compatibility from me."],"features":["Home / Showtime / Gallery workflow in the web UI for fast operation","Prebuilt action sequences for gestures, reactions, dances, and idle behavior","Real-time telemetry over Dora + Apache Arrow","Separate f